{
  "file": "./02_Knowledge/technologies/services/forgejo/backup-verification.md",
  "folder": "02_Knowledge",
  "types": {
    "source": [
      {
        "severity": "S2",
        "issue": "The note's only citation is an internal homelab wiki URL that cannot be reached, and it is the sole support for a claim about upstream Forgejo behaviour (LFS objects included in dumps). No authoritative upstream source is cited.",
        "evidence": "Line 8: `- url: \"https://wiki.homelab.local/forgejo/backup-design\"` is the single entry under `sources:`. Fetching that URL fails (transport error; `wiki.homelab.local` does not resolve from outside the homelab LAN), so the claim it is said to support on lines 24-26 cannot be checked. The behaviour in question is a `forgejo dump` default, which is documented upstream (see https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/admin/command-line/: `--skip-lfs-data  Skip LFS data`), and sibling note `./02_Knowledge/technologies/services/forgejo/operations.md` cites forgejo.org docs for the same command.",
        "fix_hint": "Add the upstream Forgejo CLI reference as a source (https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/admin/command-line/) for the dump/LFS default, and keep the internal wiki page as a secondary homelab reference. If the wiki page cannot be reached or its wording confirmed, escalate via the handoff `blocked:` field rather than asserting what it records."
      }
    ],
    "accuracy": [
      {
        "severity": "S2",
        "issue": "The note attributes LFS inclusion in the dump to the homelab's 2026 storage-layout migration. LFS data is included by `forgejo dump` as an upstream default (opted out with `--skip-lfs-data`), independent of any homelab storage change, so the stated cause will mislead a reader into thinking inclusion is contingent on that migration.",
        "evidence": "Lines 24-26: \"the dump has included LFS objects by default since the storage layout was migrated in 2026, so no separate LFS export is needed before trusting a dump.\" Forgejo's CLI reference lists `--skip-lfs-data  Skip LFS data` as an opt-in skip flag on `dump` (https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/admin/command-line/), i.e. LFS is dumped unless explicitly skipped and LFS is enabled — not because of a local storage migration. The action taken (\"no separate LFS export needed\") happens to be correct, but the reason given is not.",
        "fix_hint": "State the reason correctly: `forgejo dump` includes LFS objects by default unless `--skip-lfs-data` is passed (and LFS is enabled), citing the Forgejo CLI reference; drop or re-source the 2026 storage-migration attribution."
      }
    ],
    "scope": [],
    "structure": [
      {
